From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: fix EDMA TX DMA lifecycle

Track every streaming TX DMA mapping in a descriptor-indexed sidecar.
Completion and teardown can then unmap the exact DMA address and length by
using the matching API. This also covers every scatter-gather descriptor
instead of leaking mappings whose completion carries the MORE bit.

Pair descriptor and completion rings explicitly and account completions
through BQL. Derive the charge queue from the descriptor ring even for VP
injection, and account bytes before the producer doorbell so completion on
another CPU cannot outrun the charge. Use the core stop/recheck/wake protocol to close the ring-full
lost wakeup window. Retain error and queue-pressure counters.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
